{"codec":"JSON-syntax-dictionary-v4","atoms":["\"audit\"","\"classification\"","\"company\"","\"compounder\"","\"factors\"","\"framework\"","\"gates\"","\"history\"","\"market\"","\"missingness\"","\"model\"","\"multiples\"","\"overall_material_confidence\"","\"peers\"","\"price_cutoff\"","\"rank_bucket\"","\"research_cutoff\"","\"return_policy\"","\"scenario_summary\"","\"schema\"","\"score_sensitivity_formula_only\"","\"scores\"","\"sources\"","\"audit_scope\"","\"findings\"","\"gate_implication\"","\"restatement_vintages\"","\"Complete original FY21/FY22 standalone, FY23–FY26 consolidated and FY26 standalone audits, annexures and notes inspected; restated FY24–FY26 statements from September16 prospectus are main modeled base. Primary PDFs privately inspected, not redistributed.\"","\"current_status\"","\"finding\"","\"id\"","\"location\"","\"FY26 standalone CARO reports maintained PPE records, physical checks and no material inventory discrepancy; later audit evidence is improvement, not erasure of history.\"","\"Early opinions qualify or use subject-to wording for unaccounted AS15 gratuity and MSME interest. FY22 CARO says PPE records/physical-verification and inventory verification documentation were not produced. This is recurrent historical control weakness, not automatically proof of misappropriation.\"","\"audit_old\"","\"FY21 audit p1; FY22 audit pp1,7–8,16; FY23 audit pp1–7; prospectus pp163–164\"","\"audit2021\"","\"audit2022\"","\"audit2023\"","\"audit2024c\"","\"prospectus\"","\"FY26 original opinion unmodified; IFC effective and audit trail reported operated/preserved. Original FY25 first-page opinion is unmodified while prospectus describes FY24/FY25 reports as modified. This wording difference remains explicit.\"","\"audit_current\"","\"FY26 opinion/IFC, standalone CARO; prospectus p163\"","\"audit2026c\"","\"audit2026s\"","\"audit2025c\"","\"numbers\"","\"FY26 Q4 books minus bank statement differences: inventory5.6734cr, receivables12.7956cr, payables6.2887cr. Management explains unclosed quarterly books, year-end adjustments and net advances; explanation does not itself reconcile each difference to cash or sanction drawing power.\"","\"bank_returns\"","\"Prospectus pp178–179; FY22 Annexure C p16; FY26 standalone Annexure C\"","\"fy22_q4_debtors_bank_thousand\"","\"fy22_q4_debtors_books_thousand\"","\"fy22_q4_debtors_difference_thousand\"","\"fy22_stock_book_comparison\"","\"fy26_q4_ar_bank\"","\"fy26_q4_ar_books\"","\"fy26_q4_inventory_bank\"","\"fy26_q4_inventory_books\"","\"fy26_q4_payable_bank\"","\"fy26_q4_payable_books\"","\"122777.66\"","\"152672.45\"","\"29894.79\"","\"ND: Annexure C says not available; do not invent reconciliation.\"","\"60.4163\"","\"73.2119\"","\"20.2383\"","\"25.9117\"","\"37.2298\"","\"43.5185\"","\"note\"","\"SHR Powers purchases44.7038cr, sales2.2731cr and advances1.4209cr; FY26 Annexure D identifies an advance in nature of loan with undefined terms. CARO iii(c–e) cannot comment on repayment regularity/overdues, while iii(f) says no terms-unspecified related advances. This internal inconsistency requires clarification.\"","\"rpt\"","\"Prospectus pp56–58,199,204; FY26 standalone CARO iii and Annexure D\"","\"Haryana Power partnership is consolidated; Haryana Power proprietary/HUF services counterparty is separate. Related-party asset sale price units ambiguous; no expected sale cash assumed.\"","\"dievam_salary\"","\"related_rent\"","\"renu_property_advance\"","\"sanjeev_bonus_leave\"","\"sanjeev_remuneration\"","\"shr_advance\"","\"shr_purchase\"","\"shr_sales\"","\".48\"","\".468\"","\".31\"","\".0125\"","\"1.5\"","\"1.4209\"","\"44.7038\"","\"2.2731\"","\"status\"","\"June funded row sum29.7773cr versus printed total26.1274cr:3.6499cr difference almost exactly May2026 LAP3.65cr. Old LAP balance7.3648 differs from objects table7.4134. Model uses March audited obligations plus explicit May draw and June CC bridge, not printed total.\"","\"debt\"","\"pp90,211–213\"","\"cc_june\"","\"cc_rate\"","\"cc_sanction\"","\"funded_row_sum\"","\"new_lap\"","\"printed_total\"","\"unreconciled\"","\"17.0017\"","\".1145\"","\"22.5\"","\"29.7773\"","\"3.65\"","\"26.1274\"","\"3.6499\"","\"No March default reported. Sanctioned limits and rating opinion are not verified October available drawdowns.\"","\"retention\"","\"Performance/vendor bank guarantees17.4788cr, versus4.1673cr FY25. Margin/security deposits6.3066cr are not available cash. Full guarantee call would exceed FY26 free cash and needs separate stress; existing March guarantee is not a new financing draw.\"","\"guarantees\"","\"pp37,207; FY26 Annexure D\"","\"capital_commitments\"","\"late_delivery\"","\"restricted_deposits_and_security\"","\"warranty_closing\"","\"warranty_settled\"","\"46.7575\"","\"17.4788\"","\"2.6384\"","\"6.3066\"","\".4744\"","\".9058\"","\"Contract-by-contract retention amount, timing and guarantee-release schedule ND. Do not treat billed receivable days as the whole cash exposure.\"","\"Missing pre2006 ROC forms, pre2017 minutes and pre2010 transfer deeds; past filing errors and delays disclosed. No outstanding criminal/material litigation stated; voluntary strike-off connection does not itself evidence misconduct.\"","\"recordkeeping\"","\"pp28–29\"","\"Issuer reports exclusion from three successive PVVNL tenders under June20 2019 order. FY25/FY26 delayed-delivery charges3.2017/2.6384cr. ISO/BIS/BEE and in-house testing establish eligibility capabilities, not protected pricing or guaranteed future tender access.\"","\"qualification_execution\"","\"pp22,124,203\"","\"G1 conditional with no proven severe abuse; G2 hold for current bank-return/debt/loan inconsistencies; no favorable investability conclusion merely because FY26 audit is unmodified.\"","\"2025\"","\"2026\"","\"basis\"","\"cfo\"","\"equity\"","\"owners_pat\"","\"pat\"","\"source_id\"","\"FY26 original comparative\"","\"5.3622\"","\"44.5012\"","\"Restated PAT20.3767 differs by-0.3870cr; original employee benefits7.9128 vs restated7.6513, prior-period items0.1067 and prior-year tax0.4322 require vintage-specific review. Not cash added to valuation.\"","\"20.7630\"","\"20.7637\"","\"balance_bridge\"","\"dta\"","\"investment_property\"","\"ocl\"","\"other_current_assets\"","\"pages\"","\"ppe\"","\"restated_pat_bridge\"","\"revenue\"","\"short_provisions\"","\"Investment property0.7883 is removed and PPE increases0.7502, consistent with reclassification net of accumulated depreciation0.0381, but no explicit complete issuer reconciliation is provided. Equity declines0.1782; all remaining balance differences are preserved, not invented away.\"","\"14.8871\"","\".2505\"","\"77.5941\"","\".7883\"","\"11.3273\"","\".6375\"","\"8–10,30\"","\"33.3531\"","\"39.8193\"","\"incremental_depreciation\"","\"original_pat\"","\"remove_prior_year_tax\"","\"restated_pat\"","\"-.0022\"","\".2539\"","\"33.6048\"","\"363.1082\"","\"1.6520\"","\"Hold — unresolved; manufacturing growth/reinvestment research candidate, not evidence-backed compounder\"","\"authorized_shares\"","\"bse_code\"","\"cin\"","\"face_value\"","\"fresh_ipo_shares\"","\"isin\"","\"listing_date\"","\"listing_segment\"","\"lot_size\"","\"notes\"","\"official_interop_crosscheck\"","\"ofs_shares\"","\"pre_ipo_shares\"","\"promoter_group_percent\"","\"promoter_group_shares\"","\"prospectus_outstanding_convertibles\"","\"prospectus_promoter_pledge\"","\"public_percent\"","\"sanjeev_shares\"","\"shares\"","\"source_ids\"","\"symbol\"","25000000","\"544924\"","\"U31103DL1995PLC184910\"","\"Raksan Transformers Limited\"","\"10\"","4412800","\"INE1S7M01017\"","\"2026-09-18\"","\"BSE SME\"","400","\"NSE interoperability does not establish an NSE listing.\"","\"18:1 FY26 bonus changes share count, not economic ownership. Fresh issue diluted old holders; OFS did not fund the company.\"","\"gzip_sha256\"","\"limitation\"","\"raw_csv_sha256\"","\"rows\"","\"source_url\"","\"d3665d120c8b0379df3483321ad45f8230535c7124b9759de5c29961df326898\"","\"Interoperability metadata, not an NSE listing, a BSE current trading restriction interpretation, or a price/turnover series.\"","\"6d41d331c8f7270758a9a6aa58e679b1bed4e5d6e7cc1c9b514ec2958bfdd594\"","\"ISIN\"","\"IssdCptl\"","\"NewBrdLotQty\"","\"SctySrs\"","\"TckrSymb\"","\"2.08934000000000E+07\"","\"400\"","\"SM\"","\"RAKSAN$\"","\"ST\"","\"https://nsearchives.nseindia.com/content/cm/interop/NSE_CM_security_19102026.csv.gz\"","1100000","16480600","\"73.61\"","15380600","\"None disclosed\"","\"26.39\"","13003662","20893400","\"shareholding\"","\"capital_reconciliation\"","\"nse_interop_20261019\"","\"RAKSAN\"","false","\"BAL\"","\"CAP\"","\"CASH\"","\"D\"","\"DUR\"","\"EARN\"","\"EXEC\"","\"GOV\"","\"L\"","\"MOAT\"","\"P\"","\"R\"","\"REV\"","\"confidence\"","\"contrary\"","\"evidence_ids\"","\"facts\"","\"score\"","\"Medium\"","\"Net proceeds earmarked for capex/WC/debt, almost no March free cash, callable CC, guarantee commitments and June debt-total discrepancy constrain stress resilience.\"","\"allotment\"","\"September fresh IPO gross120.47cr, net modeled108.74cr, substantially increases funding.\"","\"March debt20.74cr is below one year EBITDA, with no reported default.\"","5","\"Prior margin/utilization improvement is not new-project IRR; ₹72.58cr project plus higher working capital means reinvestment returns not yet proven, especially with restatement/capital-payable bridge limits.\"","\"capacity\"","\"FY24–26 observed incremental NOPAT exceeds incremental invested capital cost benchmark.\"","\"Expanded power mix and utilization show existing assets earning more.\"","6","\"CFO stayed positive across all three restated years and improvedFY26; growth explains assets, not automatic cash discipline. Poor realization persists across three profitable years, so GQS cap5 applies.\"","\"FY24–26 CFO/PAT ratio of sums≈0.45, not average of annual ratios.\"","\"Receivables rose20.12→73.21cr and original/recast FCF remains thin/negative cumulatively.\"","3","\"Fresh equity and tangible operating capacity provide some cushion; stress breach is not evidence of actual insolvency.\"","\"Guarantee/receivable/working-capital/capex stresses can produce a cash shortfall.\"","\"Whole-share rescues consume bounded bank/equity capacity, are not assured.\"","4","\"Tenders can cancel/defer; 58.56% UP revenue and new capacity qualification/commissioning not yet achieved.\"","\"June2026 confirmed order estimate329.68cr and83orders provides specific demand visibility.\"","\"New project adds1900MVA power and704MVA inverter-duty capacity, planned December2026.\"","\"Margin expansion while manufactured growth slows, original-to-restated PAT adjustment and weak cash conversion reduce durability; CFO concern scored separately inCASH.\"","\"FY26 restated operating EBITDA growth is largely operating rather than other-income driven.\"","\"Owners PAT improved20.38→33.60cr despite IPO-equivalent EPS denominator dilution.\"","\"Delay penalties recur; new plant promised December2026 is not delivered as of cutoff; 2019 qualification exclusion remains part of history.\"","\"Physical throughput and power-transformer mix increased sharplyFY24–FY25.\"","\"FY26 plant utilization exceeds90% for both main product classes.\"","\"FY26 unmodified audit/effective IFC and later physical verification are improvements; no severe diversion established.\"","\"Historical audit qualifications and FY22 missing verification documentation are recurrent.\"","\"SHR related purchases44.70cr plus terms-undefined advance1.42cr and bank-return discrepancies require scrutiny.\"","\"Low\"","\"Official postlisting turnover, spread, circuit/restriction state not established. Missing observations are ND, prelisting NA.\"","\"400share lot verified; reference cost104200rupees.\"","\"ListingSeptember18 leaves short trading history.\"","null","\"Lowest-bid tenders, weak bargaining and 2019 temporary exclusion prevent a durable-pricing-moat conclusion.\"","\"BIS/BEE qualification and in-house testing support participation.\"","\"Two operating plants and repeat government utility customers demonstrate useful execution capability.\"","\"Entry cash/commitments unreconciled and conditional terminal results cannot establish a supported valuation cushion.\"","\"Reference market cap and reported multiples are calculated.\"","\"Earned terminal value requires reinvestment and self-funding, not arbitrary PE.\"","\"Current October funding/timing not verified; cash-cleared conditional branches are not a defensible unconditional return estimate.\"","\"Complete funded and unfunded counterfactual paths built.\"","\"Base pre-entry/intraperiod cash can breach before IPO even with positive terminal accounting cash.\"","\"Latest manufactured sales growth4.34%, versus12.00% headline growth; five-year FY21 standalone/COVID series is context only, not the scored basis. Original/restated GAAP and unseparated price/service/mix limit confidence. Starting three-year ≥30% schedule9, limited to8 by Medium-confidence ceiling; no second discretionary haircut.\"","\"Scored window FY23–FY26 reported consolidated nominal revenue72.367795→363.1082cr, CAGR71.20%; not organic. Removing new FY26 trading gives endpoint337.7289cr and CAGR67.11%, still≥30% band.\"","\"Manufactured transformer revenue160.19→322.53→336.52cr; trading separately removed.\"","\"Physical distribution output822278→1375253KVA and power305.85→1285MVA support real expansion.\"","8","\"calculation\"","\"name\"","\"sector_rubric\"","\"sha256\"","\"version\"","\"Decimal precision 36, ROUND_HALF_UP one-decimal displayed scores; integer 1–10 factors; NS not renormalized\"","\"Small-Micro-Cap-Stock-Research-Master-Prompt-v3.0.md\"","\"Capital-intensive transformer manufacturing; revenue checked against same-perimeter manufactured sales and physical output, not trading or commodity pass-through alone.\"","\"68d4de4255427df276318d0231530b867a453e740c74150e9768bf1387224137\"","\"3.0\"","\"G1\"","\"G2\"","\"G3\"","\"G4\"","\"r